2026-10-08 17:43:29.800 DEBUG icod.agent.runtime.loop: STEP 2: model responded ->\n  - text: ## Complete Backend API Summary\n\n### 1. All Endpoints\n\nAll routes are behind JWT auth (`Bearer` token → `req.user = { id, email }`).\n\n#### Sheets (`sheets.routes.js`)\n\n| Method | Path | Handler | Request | Response |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|----------|\n| POST | `/workspaces/:workspaceId/sheets` | `create` | `{ name: string }` | `201 { data: Sheet }` |\n| GET | `/workspaces/:workspaceId/sheets` | `listByWorkspace` | — | `{ data: Sheet[], count: number }` |\n| GET | `/sheets/:id` | `getById` | — | `{ data: Sheet }` (includes `columns[]` ordered by position + `_count.rows`) |\n| PUT | `/sheets/:id` | `update` | `{ name: string }` | `{ data: Sheet }` |\n| DELETE | `/sheets/:id` | `remove` | — | `204` |\n\n#### Columns (`columns.routes.js`)\n\n| Method | Path | Handler | Request | Response |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|----------|\n| POST | `/:sheetId/columns` | `create` | `{ name, type, position? }` | `201 { data: Column }` |\n| GET | `/:sheetId/columns` | `listBySheet` | — | `{ data: Column[], count }` |\n| PUT | `/:sheetId/columns/:columnId` | `update` | `{ name?, type?, position? }` | `{ data: Column }` |\n| DELETE | `/:sheetId/columns/:columnId` | `remove` | — | `204` |\n\n#### Rows (`rows.routes.js`)\n\n| Method | Path | Handler | Request | Response |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|----------|\n| POST | `/:sheetId/rows` | `create` | `{ values: object }` | `201 { data: Row }` |\n| GET | `/:sheetId/rows` | `listBySheet` | — | `{ data: Row[], count }` |\n| GET | `/:sheetId/rows/:rowId` | `getById` | — | `{ data: Row }` |\n| PUT | `/:sheetId/rows/:rowId` | `update` | `{ values: object }` | `{ data: Row }` (full replace, not merge) |\n| DELETE | `/:sheetId/rows/:rowId` | `remove` | — | `204` |\n\n---\n\n### 2. Data Models\n\n**Sheet** — `{ id, name, workspaceId, createdAt, updatedAt }`\n- `getById` enriches with `columns[]` (ordered by position) and `_count.rows`\n\n**Column** — `{ id, sheetId, name, type, position, createdAt, updatedAt }`\n- Unique constraints: `(sheetId, name)` and `(sheetId, position)` — both return `409` on conflict\n\n**Row** — `{ id, sheetId, values, createdAt, updatedAt }`\n- `values` is a JSON object keyed by **column ID (as string)** → typed cell value\n- Example: `{ "3": "hello", "5": 42, "7": true, "8": "2025-01-15" }`\n\n---\n\n### 3. Column Types & Validation (`rows.service.js:46-77`)\n\n| Type | JS Validation | Accepted Input |\n|------|--------------|----------------|\n| `TEXT` | `typeof === 'string'` | Any string |\n| `NUMBER` | `typeof === 'number' && isFinite()` | Finite numbers only |\n| `BOOLEAN` | `typeof === 'boolean'` | `true` / `false` |\n| `DATE` | `typeof === 'string'` + `new Date()` must be valid | ISO date strings |\n\n- Unknown column IDs in `values` → `BadRequestError`\n- All validation errors are collected and thrown as a single `400` with joined messages\n- Validation runs on both **create** and **update**\n\n---\n\n### 4. Constraints & Gotchas\n\n1. **No pagination** on any list endpoint (rows or columns)\n2. **No bulk/batch operations** — rows and columns are CRUD one-at-a-time\n3. **Row update is full replace** of `values`, not a merge\n4. **Column position conflicts** — reordering requires careful sequencing; no dedicated reorder endpoint\n5. **Column name uniqueness** per sheet enforced at DB level (P2002)\n6. **Auto-positioning**: if `position` is omitted on column create, it appends (`max + 1`)\n7. **Ownership chain**: every operation asserts ownership up the chain (workspace → sheet → column/row)\n\n---\n\n### 5. Frontend `api.js`\n\n- Raw axios instance with `baseURL` from `VITE_API_URL`\n- Auto-attaches JWT from `localStorage`\n- 401 response → clears token, redirects to `/login`\n- **No endpoint-specific helper functions** — consumers build paths manually (e.g., `api.get(\`/${sheetId}/rows\`)`)\n\n---\n\n### Key Gaps for Spreadsheet View\n\n